WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Sprig 0.1.2 Preview · Opening the app.
Capture is OFF; no VPN is started.

00:10.000 --> 00:24.000
Full prominent disclosure is shown before VPN access.
Traffic may contain personal data; history stays in app memory.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.000
Cancel: disclosure declined.
VPN remains OFF.

00:28.000 --> 00:34.000
The app is reopened and Start capture is selected again.
The disclosure is shown again.

00:34.000 --> 00:42.000
Agree and continue requests Android VPN permission.
System dialog: Sprig requests permission to monitor network traffic.

00:42.000 --> 00:52.000
Android system consent is pending.
Cancel and OK are available; VPN has not started.

00:52.000 --> 00:56.000
OK: Android VPN permission granted.
Sprig starts its local VpnService; the VPN key icon appears.

00:56.000 --> 01:00.000
Only a local test app is selected for capture.
20 test requests completed with zero errors.

01:00.000 --> 01:06.000
VPN is running: 20 requests appear in HTTP history with status 200.
Requests reach the chosen local test server; history stays on device.

01:06.000 --> 01:10.110
Stop capture: VPN is stopped by the user.
Local address and test token are masked; footage runs at normal speed.
